From ace50346094a9fa4898a46c103ab9f05a760dfe1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suiyan <suiyan@sunmmio.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 05:10:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] dadao: add arch/dadao compile-time skeleton (ML-009a)

Adds the musl arch port directory for DADAO: syscall_arch.h (rd16=sysno,
rd17-22=args, rd31=return, `trap 2, 0` per ADR-0014 D2), reloc.h (mapped
against contracts/elf/spec.md's 10 relocation types, not the legacy
~/toolchain/musl numbering), bits/alltypes.h.in + bits/stdint.h (64-bit,
big-endian per contracts/elf/spec.md EI_DATA), bits/syscall.h.in (asm-generic
numbering matching the already-implemented cfx_smon trap responders),
bits/{float,stat,signal,setjmp,posix}.h and kstat.h, plus the missing
`dadao*) ARCH=dadao` configure rule.

Verified: `./configure --target=dadao` completes; 766 of ~1600 candidate
.c files across the tree (all of src/string's non-tail-call functions, most
of src/stdio, etc.) compile cleanly with clang --target=dadao. Remaining
failures are out of this task's scope: atomic_arch.h (deferred to a
pthread/atomic follow-up task) and pre-existing DADAO LLVM backend codegen
gaps (soft-float libcalls, tail-call lowering, dynamic_stackalloc) unrelated
to these musl headers.
